  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "OpenccNetLib v1.2.0\n\nThis release focuses on performance and code simplification.\n\nBenchmarks (BenchmarkDotNet 0.15.2, .NET 9.0.8, Win11, X64 RyuJIT AVX2; IterationCount=10, WarmupCount=1):\n- 100 chars: 2.49–2.50 µs, ~5.5 KB allocated\n- 1,000 chars: ~57.8 µs, ~84.0 KB allocated\n- 10,000 chars: ~305.9 µs, ~798.7 KB allocated\n- 100,000 chars: ~6.74 ms, ~8.39 MB allocated\n- 1,000,000 chars: ~65.17 ms, ~84.93 MB allocated\nCompared to v1.0.3 FMM-only: up to ~4.3× faster on short inputs and ~70% less allocation across sizes.\n\nHighlights\n- Added StarterUnion with union + plan caching (ConversionPlanCache) → reduces big array churn, fewer Gen2/LOH collections.\n- O(1) starter metadata: per-starter cap + 64-bit length mask + minLen → skips impossible probe lengths.\n- Correct longest-match behavior: single-grapheme fast path only when no longer candidates exist.\n- Surrogate-aware emit path (.NET Standard 2.0 safe) and astral-safe indexing.\n- Avalonia GUI memory stabilized (~250 MB vs. prior ~400 MB under similar workloads).\n\nTechnical Notes\n- Removed legacy StarterCapTextElem and BuildStarterIndex path (now redundant).\n- Primary cache: (config, punctuation) → DictRefs (with per-round unions).\n- Secondary cache: round layout (BaseDictId[]) → shared StarterUnion.\n- Mask+cap+minLen clamping reduces probe attempts and avoids tiny string churn.\n- Reuse of StringBuilder + ArrayPool<char> lowers GC pressure.\n\nProject: https://github.com/laisuk/OpenccNet",
